--TEST--
a type-parameter name of an `extend` block may not be a name its file resolves to a type: `Tag` and `Item` are classes of the file, so each is `E0338`, and the help suggests a name such as `K` — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;

use Core\ObjectMap;

class Tag {}

class Item {}

extend ObjectMap<Tag, Item> as Index {
    public function size(): uint {
        return $this->count();
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
// covers: lang:classes/extend-blocks
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0338]: `Tag` names the type `App\Tag`, so it cannot name a type parameter
   --> %s:10:18
   |
10 | extend ObjectMap<Tag, Item> as Index {
   |                  ^^^ this name is already a type in this file
   = help: pick a name that is not a type, such as `K`. Inside the block, the name is the type argument of each value

error[E0338]: `Item` names the type `App\Item`, so it cannot name a type parameter
   --> %s:10:23
   |
10 | extend ObjectMap<Tag, Item> as Index {
   |                       ^^^^ this name is already a type in this file
   = help: pick a name that is not a type, such as `K`. Inside the block, the name is the type argument of each value

error: aborting due to 2 errors
